 " -", "lp": -0.001264119055122137, "top": [[" -", -0.001264119055122137], [" ...", -6.8428568840026855]]}, {"t": "DC", "lp": -0.00024339537776540965, "top": [["DC", -0.00024339537776540965], ["D", -8.575736045837402]]}, {"t": "MAKE", "lp": -2.8133788873674348e-05, "top": [["MAKE", -2.8133788873674348e-05], ["Make", -11.587983131408691]]}, {"t": "_INSTALL", "lp": -0.08716195821762085, "top": [["_INSTALL", -0.08716195821762085], ["_C", -2.5031490325927734]]}, {"t": "_PREFIX", "lp": -0.00016344929463230073, "top": [["_PREFIX", -0.00016344929463230073], ["_LIB", -10.562385559082031]]}, {"t": "=/", "lp": -6.234840111574158e-05, "top": [["=/", -6.234840111574158e-05], ["=${", -10.77637004852295]]}, {"t": "usr", "lp": -2.0742631022585556e-05, "top": [["usr", -2.0742631022585556e-05], [" -", -12.362868309020996]]}], "text": "Here is a step-by-step breakdown of the `build()` function in your PKGBUILD.\n\n### 1. Environment Setup\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\nset -e\n```\n*   **`source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force`**: This script sets up the environment variables required for Intel OneAPI tools (like `icx`, `icpx`, and MKL libraries) to work correctly. The `--force` flag ensures that if these variables are already set, they are overwritten with the current OneAPI version's settings.\n*   **`set -e`**: This is a standard bash safety measure. It causes the script to exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero exit code (an error). This prevents the build from continuing with broken state if a previous step failed.\n\n### 2. CMake Configuration\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n*   **`cmake`**: Invokes the CMake build system generator.\n*   **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`**: Specifies the **source directory**. This is where the downloaded git repository code lives.\n*   **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`**: Specifies the **build directory**. CMake will generate all intermediate files (object files, makefiles, etc.) here, keeping the source directory clean.\n*   **`-G Ninja`**: Specifies the **build system generator**. Instead of using `make`, it uses `Ninja`, which is generally faster and better at parallel builds.\n\n### 3. Compiler and Build Type Flags\n```bash\n    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr"}